{"uid":"210615487562823f","name":"test_header_makes_no_self_skip_claim_about_the_docker_or_browser_tiers","fullName":"tests.test_host_like_pytest_script#test_header_makes_no_self_skip_claim_about_the_docker_or_browser_tiers","historyId":"09f1c033aaa21006ca19687a723451b5","time":{"start":1791889690021,"stop":1791889690028,"duration":7},"description":"F2 (#74): an earlier header claimed a usable docker socket is always\n    present here, so the docker tier is always filtered out and self-skip\n    is dismissed outright as a false premise -- itself false, since socket\n    presence genuinely varies per invocation (some ralphd job containers\n    have one, some -- including this one -- do not, and a bare developer\n    host usually has none). The header's actual, current behaviour branches\n    on that per-invocation probe: when a usable socket IS present it\n    injects ``-m \"not docker\"`` to filter the tier out (never runs it\n    nested); when the socket is ABSENT it injects nothing, and the\n    docker-marked modules' own module-level ``skipif`` self-skips cleanly,\n    the same as it would for a developer running the bare command by hand.\n    The header must describe *both* branches, cite #74, and must not claim\n    either branch -- present or absent -- as this environment's\n    unconditional, universal behaviour.","descriptionHtml":"<p>F2 (#74): an earlier header claimed a usable docker socket is always<br />\npresent here, so the docker tier is always filtered out and self-skip<br />\nis dismissed outright as a false premise -- itself false, since socket<br />\npresence genuinely varies per invocation (some ralphd job containers<br />\nhave one, some -- including this one -- do not, and a bare developer<br />\nhost usually has none). The header's actual, current behaviour branches<br />\non that per-invocation probe: when a usable socket IS present it<br />\ninjects <code>-m &quot;not docker&quot;</code> to filter the tier out (never runs it<br />\nnested); 